# Testing — vitest, colocated, public API only

## Context

Tests are colocated `*.test.ts` files next to their unit
(`app/src/reducer.test.ts`, `app/src/store.test.ts`,
`app/src/lib/text.test.ts`) and run with vitest via `cd app && npm test`.
They are the safety net that makes the do-not-touch and architecture rules
mechanically checkable.

## Rule

- Use vitest ONLY; put every new test in a colocated `*.test.ts` next to the
  module under test (a test for `app/src/selectors.ts` lives at
  `app/src/selectors.test.ts`).
- Structure each test as Arrange–Act–Assert: build state or `createStore()`,
  dispatch or call the function, then assert on `getState()` or the return
  value.
- Test through the public API: `dispatch` + `getState`, or the exported
  reducer/selector/lib functions. DO NOT reach into store internals or
  re-implement reducer logic inside a test.
- Every new `Action` variant gets at least one reducer test covering its
  state transition.
- Keep existing tests green. Update an exact-shape expectation (e.g.
  `toEqual({ id, title, done: false })`) ONLY when the domain shape
  legitimately changed (e.g. `Task` gained `priority`), and say so explicitly
  in the PR description.

## How to verify

1. `cd app && npm test` → all suites pass.
2. Every `case "..."` string in `app/src/reducer.ts` appears in at least one test in `app/src/reducer.test.ts` (grep each action `type` string).
3. `grep -rnE "as any|\(store as" app/src/*.test.ts app/src/lib/*.test.ts` → zero matches (no poking at internals).
